<title>BRAZIL: Brazil soybean crop 96 pct harvested - Safras.</title>
<headline>Brazil soybean crop 96 pct harvested - Safras.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Around 96 percent of Brazil's expected soybean crop had been harvested by May 1, consultants Safras e Mercado said in a weekly report.</p>
<p>The 96 percent compares with 89 percent by May 2, 1996, and a historical average over the past five years of 85 percent, it added.</p>
<p>A breakdown of percentage harvested by state follows.</p>
<p> STATE		     01/05/97   24/04/97   02/05/96  5-yr avge</p>
<p> Rio Grande do Sul	 95	    86	   75	  77</p>
<p> Parana		     100	    98	   98	  96</p>
<p> Mato Grosso		 98	    95	   97	  94</p>
<p> Mato Grosso do Sul	99	    96	   99	  93</p>
<p> Goias			 97	    90	   96	  77</p>
<p> Sao Paulo		  100	   100	  100	  98</p>
<p> Minas Gerais		73	    62	   75	  61</p>
<p> Others			90	    74	   76	  73</p>
<p> TOTAL BRAZIL		96	    90	   89	  85</p>
<p>((-Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151))</p>
